Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(training):=20workouts=20told=20in=20your?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20own=20words=20=E2=80=94=20live=20sets=20to=20tick,=20past=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?sessions=20with=20their=20time,=20Claude's=20energy=20estimate?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Start and Add open a words-first sheet: say (on-device dictation) or type the
workout, Claude turns it into exercises and sets, the wearer corrects them.
'About to train' starts the live workout with every set as a row to tick (the
tick times split the strap's heart rate by exercise); 'Already trained' saves a
manual workout for the said time, so the strap's heart rate for that window
fills it in. Upstream's sport picker and manual form stay one tap away.

When a session ends Claude estimates its energy from the sets, reps and loads,
the profile and smart scale, and the strap's heart rate. Only what exceeds the
larger of the heart-rate figure and the resting share of the window is added
to the day's burn (food balance, history, Today card), so nothing is counted
twice and steady cardio adds nothing. The workout detail shows the exercises,
heart rate per exercise, both figures and lets the sets be edited; the AI
Coach gets a TRAINING LOG line.

Fork-owned package com.noop.training (JSON store paired to the workout row by
startTs + sport); upstream touched by one-line hooks: endWorkout/discardWorkout,
the live screen, the Start/Add buttons and the detail sheet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
